<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Siena at Montalcino</h1><p class="st-meta">1555 CE – 1559 CE · capital Montalcino</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last stand of the Sienese republic, kept alive in the hill town of Montalcino with French support for four years after Siena fell.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-siena">Siena</a> surrendered to imperial and Florentine forces in April 1555, several hundred citizens who refused to submit withdrew to the fortified town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montalcino">Montalcino</a>, south of the city, and continued the government of the Republic of Siena there under French protection.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The exiles kept the republic's magistracies and seal, minted coins and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montalcino">Montalcino</a> and a few nearby towns. They depended on French troops and on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piero-strozzi">Piero Strozzi</a>, the Florentine exile who commanded for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Tuscany</a>. The republic's territory was small, its resources were slight and it lived under the constant threat of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-florence">Duchy of Florence</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-cateau-cambresis">Peace of Cateau-Cambrésis</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1559 withdrew French support, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montalcino">Montalcino</a> surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a>, joining the future <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Grand Duchy of Tuscany</a>. The town's people are still nicknamed the last Sienese.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1555 CE – 1559 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M